# Glama MCP Python API Docs | dltHub

Build a Glama MCP-to-database pipeline in Python using dlt with AI Workbench support for Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex.

Last updated: May 31, 2026

Glama's MCP server dynamically translates OpenAPI specifications into MCP tools. The server is hosted at [https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gujord/OpenAPI-MCP](https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gujord/OpenAPI-MCP). The current version is available at [https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gujord/OpenAPI-MCP/tree/68a127c457712c2aaf7cc74409ac83b9a003c05f/test](https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gujord/OpenAPI-MCP/tree/68a127c457712c2aaf7cc74409ac83b9a003c05f/test). The REST API base URL is `https://glama.ai/api/mcp/v1` and No authentication is required for the public MCP endpoints..

dlt is an open-source Python library that handles authentication, pagination, and schema evolution automatically. dlthub provides AI context files that enable code assistants to generate production-ready pipelines. Install with `uv add "dlt[hub]"` and start loading Glama MCP data in under 10 minutes.

---

## What data can I load from Glama MCP?

