## How do I authenticate with the Glama MCP API?

Requests can be made without any authentication headers.

**1\. Get your credentials**

No credentials are needed; the API is publicly accessible.

**2\. Add them to `.dlt/secrets.toml`**

Copy

`[sources.glama_mcp_source]`

dlt reads this automatically at runtime — never hardcode tokens in your pipeline script. For production environments, see [setting up credentials with dlt](https://dlthub.com/docs/walkthroughs/add_credentials) for environment variable and vault-based options.

---

## How do I set up and run the pipeline?

**Set up a virtual environment and install dlt:**

Copy

`uv init uv add "dlt[hub]"`

**1\. Install the `dlt` AI Workbench:**

Copy

`uv run dlthub ai init --agent <your-agent> # <agent>: claude | cursor | codex`

This installs project rules, a secrets management skill, appropriate ignore files, and configures the `dlt` MCP server for your agent. [Learn more →](https://dlthub.com/docs/dlt-ecosystem/llm-tooling/llm-native-workflow)

**2\. Install the `rest-api-pipeline` toolkit:**

Copy

`uv run dlthub ai toolkit install rest-api-pipeline`

This loads the skills and context about `dlt` the agent uses to build the pipeline iteratively, efficiently, and safely. The agent uses MCP tools to inspect credentials — it never needs to read your `secrets.toml` directly. [Learn more →](https://dlthub.com/docs/dlt-ecosystem/llm-tooling/llm-native-workflow#anatomy-of-the-toolkit)

**3\. Start LLM-assisted coding:**

```
Use /find-source to load data from the Glama MCP API into DuckDB.
```

The **`rest-api-pipeline`** toolkit takes over from here — it reads relevant API documentation, presents you with options for which endpoints to load, and follows a structured workflow to scaffold, debug, and validate the pipeline step by step.

**4\. Run the pipeline:**

Copy

`uv run python glama_mcp_pipeline.py`

If everything is configured correctly, you'll see output like this:

Copy

`Pipeline glama_mcp_pipeline load step completed in 0.26 seconds 1 load package(s) were loaded to destination duckdb and into dataset glama_mcp_data The duckdb destination used duckdb:/glama_mcp.duckdb location to store data Load package 1749667187.541553 is LOADED and contains no failed jobs`

**Inspect your pipeline and data:**

Copy

`uv run dlthub show`

This opens the Pipeline Dashboard where you can verify pipeline state, load metrics, schema (tables, columns, types), and query the loaded data directly.

