## How do I query the loaded data?

Once the pipeline runs, dlt creates one table per resource. You can query with Python or SQL.

**Python (pandas DataFrame):**

Copy

`import dlt data = dlt.pipeline("glama_mcp_pipeline").dataset() sessions_df = data.servers.df() print(sessions_df.head())`

**SQL (DuckDB example):**

Copy

`SELECT * FROM glama_mcp_data.servers LIMIT 10;`

**In a marimo or Jupyter notebook:**

Copy

`import dlt data = dlt.pipeline("glama_mcp_pipeline").dataset() data.servers.df().head()`

See [how to explore your data in marimo Notebooks](https://dlthub.com/docs/general-usage/dataset-access/marimo) and [how to query your data in Python with dataset](https://dlthub.com/docs/general-usage/dataset-access/dataset).

